the old fashion has a pretty good claim  to being one of the most popular  cocktails of all time it's certainly one  of my favorites but even though it's  traditionally made with whiskey it's  surprisingly adaptable to lots of other  spirits so today I'm going to show you  one my favorite variations on the old  fashioned the Applejack roll is  fashioned for this cocktail you're going  to need some apple brandy some maple  syrup preferably a grade B maple syrup  it's a little bit richer some Angostura  bitters and some aromatic bitters and  then finally an orange peel for garnish  we're going to start with two ounces of  apple brandy apple Brandy's popularity  in America goes back well before the  Revolutionary War in fact the first  commercial distillery in the whole  United States  distilled apple brandy it's really great  on its own and it's excellent on  cocktails so now we're going to add a  bar spoon of maple syrup which is about  half a teaspoon really don't need very  much be careful because it can get sweet  really fast now we're gonna add our  bitters we're gonna do two dashes of  Angostura bitters which are pretty much  the most common bitters in the world  also the most useful if you only own one  brand of bitters haven't read this one  and finally I like to add a dash of  aromatic bitters aromatic bitters are a  broad category but they usually are  darker and have more baking spice notes  like cinnamon and nutmeg which obviously  are going to play great with our maple  syrup and rapid Randy all right now  we're ready to stir because this is all  alcohol over 90 to the percent alcohol  we don't want to shake it you want to  preserve that nice silky texture stir  for about 30 seconds or so I'm going to  serve this on the rocks because it's so  stiff a little extra dilution is a good  thing of course using fresh ice is  always key for really strong drinks like  this keeps them colder and now we're  gonna garnish this with an orange peel  peel a nice swamp so you just want to  pinch it lightly so the oil sprays over  the glass with all those dark earthy  notes and then it's nice to have those  aromatics from the orange oil to  brighten it up there you are and that is  the Applejack old fashioned this is a  great Thanksgiving drink  I love after the big meal sitting in  front of the fireplace sipping on one of  these surrounded by family it's  something I look forward to every year  if you like that drink subscribe to the  GQ channel for more
 

